From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Azure Dreams <azuredreams@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:14:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] HD-2D shader: tilt-shift depth of field, bloom, grading
 and vignette over sharp pixels

A four-pass chain (ShaderConfig.HD2D, SHADER_HD2D): a soft copy of the frame
at half the console's resolution that also marks the game's interface, a
Gaussian blur across and down at a quarter of it, then the screen pass, which
keeps the pixels sharp and blends the soft copy in toward the top and bottom,
adds bloom, grades the colors and darkens the corners. The passes work in the
console's pixels at any internal resolution (ShaderConfig.HD2D.resolution).

Tuned for Azure Dreams: its interface stays sharp on top of the effects while
the scene keeps its depth of field. White lettering on its windows' dark blue
fill and the deep navy of the tower's gauges are found and left alone (and
give no glow); the strip with the gauges stays sharp; and while the dialogue
window is up, it stays sharp from a little above its first line of text down,
along with the speaker's portrait beside it.
